            "application/vnd.google.colaboratory.intrinsic+json": {
              "summary": "{\n  \"name\": \"df\",\n  \"rows\": 2729,\n  \"fields\": [\n    {\n      \"column\": \"prompt\",\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"dtype\": \"category\",\n        \"num_unique_values\": 1107,\n        \"samples\": [\n          \"Some people say that people remember special gifts or presents that they receive. Why do you think that is?\",\n          \"Testing on animals is common practice for products such as cosmetics or drugs. Some people regard testing on animals as completely wrong and inhumane and they believe is should not be allowed. Do you agree or disagree with this statement?\",\n          \"Many manufactured food and drink products contain high levels of sugar, which causes many health problems. Sugary products should be made more expensive to encourage people to consume less sugar. Do you agree or disagree?\"\n        ],\n        \"semantic_type\": \"\",\n        \"description\": \"\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"column\": \"text\",\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"dtype\": \"string\",\n        \"num_unique_values\": 2729,\n        \"samples\": [\n          \"Nowadays, it is acknowledged that sport professionals earn huge salaries that exceed other respected professionals by far. This situation has sparked a heated debate with opinions on both sides, in favor and against. Some people argue that is irresponsible to pay such amount of money to people who has just borned with a natural gift to play certain sport. They believe this is unfair for other professionals that spent several years studying hard and have to deal with really serious situations daily. Doctors, engineers, fire fighters among others, are clear examples of this unbalanced situation. Furthermore, we are setting a bad example for the youngsters as they grow up witnessing how our society do not reward the hard work. Nevertheless, other people assert that athletes deserve their salary. They have a very short career, as can only play at highest performance during very limited amount of years. Normally sport players above thirty five are consider old to keep playing professionally. Moreover, they have a big responsibility as are requested to perform their best in every single game. It is their job to strive until see their team win, there are millions of dollars involved in each game. Companies invest a lot of money to sponsor teams and this creates an extra pressure on the players. In a nutshell, I believe that athletes deserve a huge compensation for their work. Even though it is true that they have been naturally gifted however they still need to train hard every day to perform their best and help the sponsors to boost their brand value hence increasing the selling.\",\n          \"In numerous regions across the globe and within various sectors, an increasing number of individuals are opting to remain at home instead of commuting to their workplaces. Critics of remote work contend that physical presence in a shared workplace with colleagues is crucial for maintaining both mental well-being and overall happiness. Prolonged isolation from interpersonal interactions may precipitate feelings of depression. Furthermore, they assert that professional development necessitates engagement in both formal and informal settings with coworkers. While it is posited that digital communication, particularly through video conferencing platforms, can facilitate interaction, detractors maintain that such virtual exchanges cannot truly substitute for direct face-to-face contact.  In my perspective, the merits of telecommuting surpass its drawbacks. Primarily, a considerable number of employees express a preference for working from home, citing enhanced productivity due to reduced stress levels and the elimination of lengthy commutes. Advances in technology have increasingly enabled individuals to connect virtually as if they were physically co-located. Additionally, diminished travel contributes to a lower carbon footprint; however, this assertion remains contentious as many individuals choose to reside in more remote areas where car usage does not significantly decline despite telecommuting arrangements.  Ultimately, I am convinced that remote work presents significant advantages by allowing greater participation in the workforce among those who might otherwise be excluded. This option proves especially liberating for women who frequently bear additional caregiving responsibilities. In conclusion, I firmly advocate that working from home represents the most equitable and efficient solution for the majority of individuals.\",\n          \"The rapid advancements in artificial intelligence (AI) have sparked a heated debate regarding their potential impact on society. While some individuals champion the benefits of AI, believing it will enhance our lives significantly, others express concerns about our readiness for a future where machines may surpass human intelligence. This essay will discuss both perspectives before presenting my own viewpoint.  Proponents of AI argue that its development can lead to numerous positive outcomes. For instance, AI has already revolutionized various sectors such as healthcare, finance, and transportation. In healthcare, algorithms can analyze vast amounts of data to identify diseases early and suggest personalized treatment plans, ultimately saving lives. Furthermore, in industries like finance, AI systems are capable of detecting fraudulent activities with greater accuracy than humans ever could. These innovations not only improve efficiency but also free up human resources for more creative and strategic tasks.  Conversely, critics raise valid concerns about the implications of advanced AI technologies. One major worry is the potential loss of jobs due to automation; as machines become more competent at performing tasks traditionally done by humans, many workers may find themselves displaced without adequate retraining opportunities. Additionally, there are fears surrounding ethical considerations and decision-making processes governed by algorithms that lack human empathy or moral judgment\\u2014issues that could lead to unintended consequences if left unchecked.  In my opinion, while the benefits of AI cannot be overlooked\\u2014especially in terms of efficiency and innovation\\u2014the risks associated with its unregulated growth must be addressed proactively. It is crucial for governments and organizations to establish guidelines that ensure ethical practices in developing these technologies while investing in education programs aimed at preparing the workforce for an increasingly automated world.  In conclusion, although developments in artificial intelligence hold great promise for enhancing our quality of life through improved services and efficiencies across various sectors, we must remain vigilant about the challenges they present. By fostering a balanced approach that embraces innovation while prioritizing ethical standards and workforce preparedness, we can harness the power of AI responsibly for future generations.\"\n        ],\n        \"semantic_type\": \"\",\n        \"description\": \"\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"column\": \"is_ai\",\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"dtype\": \"number\",\n        \"std\": 0,\n        \"min\": 0,\n        \"max\": 1,\n        \"num_unique_values\": 2,\n        \"samples\": [\n          0,\n          1\n        ],\n        \"semantic_type\": \"\",\n        \"description\": \"\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"column\": \"variant\",\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"dtype\": \"category\",\n        \"num_unique_values\": 3,\n        \"samples\": [\n          \"raw\",\n          \"paraphrased\"\n        ],\n        \"semantic_type\": \"\",\n        \"description\": \"\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"column\": \"replace_index\",\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"dtype\": \"object\",\n        \"semantic_type\": \"\",\n        \"description\": \"\"\n      }\n    }\n  ]\n}",
